commit d2a7a7250a614382ee72e74dbbc4d1b08692354e

C03: conductor command turn.memory-confirm answers the private memory channel's own confirmation (MEMORY1247)

On a fresh profile an explicit «recuerda que me llamo …» ends in
memory_disabled and the private channel asks to enable the local memory; that
confirmation belongs to the App, not the kernel, so the one-turn instrument
could not measure any save (MEMORY1245). The new command runs the request
turn and, only when the memory channel left exactly the expected challenge
pending, submits the closed reply «confirmar» as a second turn; enabling
continues the original save. The view model exposes the pending memory
confirmation to the conductor on the UI thread only. No tests (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


